          "term": "proton-proton",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "[]{#sec:nuclear-configuration label=\"sec:nuclear-configuration\"} Nuclei are complicated many-body systems of fermions, whose structure and dynamics emerge from individual interactions among the constituent protons and neutrons. To a remarkably large extent, the latter can be modeled by the non-relativistic Hamiltonian $$H=\\sum_{i}\\frac{{\\bf p}_i^2}{2m_N}+\\sum_{i<j} v_{ij}+ \\sum_{i<j<k}V_{ijk}\\,, \\label{NMBT:ham}$$",
      "extractCut": true
    },
