      ],
      "extract": "As mentioned above, when a nucleon is struck, its momentum is obtained assuming either a local or global Fermi gas distribution. In the case of the local Fermi gas, the magnitude of the three-momentum is randomly sampled in the interval $[0,k^N_F(r)]$ where $k^N_F(r)$ is the Fermi Momentum defined in terms of the single nucleon density $k^N_F(r)=(\\rho_N(r)3\\pi^3)^{1/3}$ and $N=p,n$. In the case of the global Fermi",
      "extractCut": true
