      "extract": "If an interaction occurred, the phase space of the outgoing particles is generated using fully differential nucleon-nucleon cross sections. Note that, at the moment, we only include protons and neutrons in our INC model. Pauli blocking enforces Fermi-Dirac statistics for the nucleons and amounts to testing whether their final-state momenta are above the Fermi momentum. Two different models of the Pauli exclusion",
